"authorId": "2386607457", "name": "Russ B. Altman"}, {"authorId": "2145361446", "name": "Meng-Di Wang"}, {"authorId": "2162547030", "name": "Le Cong"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "4aa138e2e5ad4cbbef1698151257fc3092f8edfe", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "journals/corr/abs-2405-19119", "DOI": "10.48550/arXiv.2405.19119", "CorpusId": 283468398}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/4aa138e2e5ad4cbbef1698151257fc3092f8edfe", "title": "Can Graph Learning Improve Task Planning?", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.48550/arXiv.2405.19119?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2405.19119, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2181344415", "name": "Xi-Xi Wu"}, {"authorId": "2301314401", "name": "Yi-Fei Shen"}, {"authorId": "2053160406", "name": "Caihua Shan"}, {"authorId": "2371389115", "name": "Kai-Tao Song"}, {"authorId": "2301380057", "name": "Si-Wei Wang"}, {"authorId": "2303657781", "name": "Bohang Zhang"}, {"authorId": "2337537781", "name": "Jia-Rui Feng"}, {"authorId": "2303800322", "name": "Hong Cheng"}, {"authorId": "2301489372", "name": "Wei Chen"}, {"authorId": "2286138434", "name": "Yun Xiong"}, {"authorId": "2315485441", "name": "Dongsheng Li"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "aa3e30063c164437745fae0e4a0cec223cae7772", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "conf/esann/BonettaZCPM24", "DOI": "10.14428/esann/2024.es2024-181", "CorpusId": 272549233}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/aa3e30063c164437745fae0e4a0cec223cae7772", "title": "Vision Language Models as Policy Learners in Reinforcement Learning Environments", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "http://dx.doi.org/10.14428/esann/2024.es2024-181", "status": "BRONZE", "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.14428/esann/2024.es2024-181?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.14428/esann/2024.es2024-181, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "66951248", "name": "Giovanni Bonetta"}, {"authorId": "2307939778", "name": "Davide Zago"}, {"authorId": "2853804", "name": "R. Cancelliere"}, {"authorId": "2320423469", "name": "Mirko Polato"}, {"authorId": "2291361020", "name": "Bernardo Magnini"}], "abstract": ". In various domains requiring general knowledge and agent reasoning, traditional reinforcement learning (RL) algorithms often start from scratch, lacking prior knowledge of the environment. This approach can lead to signi\ufb01cant ine\ufb03ciencies as agents sometimes undergo extensive exploration before optimizing their actions. Conversely, in this paper we assume that recent Vision Language Models (VLMs), integrating both visual and textual information, possess inherent knowledge and basic reasoning capabilities, o\ufb00ering potential solutions to the sample ine\ufb03ciency problem in RL. The paper explores the integration of VLMs into RL by employing a robust VLM model, Ide\ufb01cs-9B, as a policy updated via Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO). Experimental results on simulated environments demonstrate that utilizing VLMs in RL signi\ufb01cantly accelerates PPO convergence and improves rewards compared to traditional solutions. Additionally, we pro-pose a streamlined modi\ufb01cation to the model architecture for memory e\ufb03ciency and lighter training, and we release a number of upgraded environments featuring both visual observations and textual descriptions, which, we hope, will facilitate research in VLM and RL applications. Code is available at: https://github.com/giobin/VlmPolicyEsann24"}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "f455c917b10d20bfc64010c85549e36dd0fe506e", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "journals/corr/abs-2407-05434", "DOI": "10.48550/arXiv.2407.05434", "CorpusId": 284487840}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/f455c917b10d20bfc64010c85549e36dd0fe506e", "title": "LTLBench: Towards Benchmarks for Evaluating Temporal Logic Reasoning in Large Language Models", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.48550/arXiv.2407.05434?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2407.05434, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer Science"], "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2298417108", "name": "Weizhi Tang"}, {"authorId": "144893617", "name": "Vaishak Belle"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "a6a7a20a5b3bed2290be6b244e8a64b4ad08aae9", "externalIds": {"DBLP": "journals/corr/abs-2401-09851", "DOI": "10.48550/arXiv.2401.09851", "CorpusId": 285072742}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/a6a7a20a5b3bed2290be6b244e8a64b4ad08aae9", "title": "Behavioral Simulation: Exploring A Possible Next Paradigm for Science", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.48550/arXiv.2401.09851?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2401.09851, which is subject to the license by the aut